[provenance] Stated constants in effect (no tool source; each is an assumption this run rests on):
  H-tree scaling constants = reference network clock 2.0 GHz, resolution 10, reference hops 8
      governs: the NoC link latency, and with it every hierarchy traversal, on the analytical AND detailed paths
      override: (none)
  bank-group port width = the bank serialisation width x 2 (an interleaving assumption)
      governs: the L2 rung of the hierarchy link ladder: its width, its bandwidth, and every level-2 crossing derived from them
      override: (none -- no architecture object carries this field)
  bandwidth reference anchor = HBM3's per-channel and L0 bandwidth, read from its preset
      governs: per-layer link widths, Garnet link latency and flits-per-access on the detailed path
      override: (derived, not a constant -- listed so the normalisation is visible)
  MLP degree M = 10
      governs: the PE outstanding-access window in the M/D/1 model
      override: noc.mlp
  network-interface overhead = 6 cycles
      governs: the average one-way NoC latency, added for every topology including BUS and CROSSBAR where the hop count is zero
      override: (none)
  PE local-link latency = 2 cycles
      governs: the PE<->local-memory hop
      override: pim.pe.local_link_latency
  (Quantities the tools CAN answer are measured instead and are not listed here.)
